    "https://www.timeshighereducation.com/unijobs/listing/416583/lecturer-accounting/": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Accounting",
      "description": "Lecturer, Accounting job with SWINBURNE UNIVERSITY OF TECHNOLOGY | 416583 Skip to main content News Rankings Jobs Study abroad Events Resources Solutions Skip to main menu Skip to user menu Jobseekers: Login Sign up Employers: Login (This link will open in a new window) Post a\n                          job (This link will open in a new window) Employers Jobs Home Find a job Job alerts Upload CV Careers advice the.com (This link will open in a new window) More Results Lecturer, Accounting Employer SWINBURNE UNIVERSITY OF TECHNOLOGY Location Hawthorn, Australia Closing date 5 Nov 2026 View more categories View less categories Academic Discipline Business & Economics , Accounting & Finance Job Type Academic Posts , Lecturers / Assistant Professors Contract Type Permanent Hours Full Time Apply on website Save job Click to add the job to your shortlist You need to sign in or create an account to save a job. Send job Job Details Inspire future business leaders through innovative teaching and impactful research. Full-time, ongoing position at our Hawthorn campus Academic Level B salary + 17% super and staff benefits Join Swinburne University of Technology’s Department of Accounting, Economics and Finance and contribute to a vibrant academic community committed to high-quality education, research excellence and meaningful industry connections. We’re seeking a passionate and collaborative accounting academic who can inspire students, deliver engaging learning experiences and contribute to the Department’s growing research profile. About the Role As Lecturer, Accounting, you’ll deliver engaging lectures, tutorials and workshops across undergraduate and postgraduate programs, both on campus and online. You’ll play an important role in developing students’ knowledge and professional capabilities through contemporary teaching approaches, including blended learning, case studies, role-plays and simulations. You’ll also contribute to curriculum development, 